{"id":"rdb-1ced7f","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support ALTER TABLE on primary key columns (drop, type change, re-keying)","description":"ALTER TABLE currently rejects dropping or changing the type of primary key columns because PK values are binary-encoded as row keys in the prolly tree. Supporting this requires re-keying every row entry — decode all rows, rebuild the tree with new keys, update the manifest.\n\nPrerequisite: rdb-cf0385 (basic ALTER TABLE support).\n\nScope:\n- `ALTER TABLE ... DROP COLUMN` where the column is part of the PK\n- `ALTER TABLE ... MODIFY COLUMN` with a type change on a PK column\n- Re-keying all prolly tree entries with the new key encoding\n- Handling composite PKs where only one column changes","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":5,"sort_order":"aC","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-1ced7f","target_id":"rdb-cf0385","kind":"depends_on"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:44:53.267195Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-68106e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Support DEFAULT values for columns","description":"There is no support for column DEFAULT values. This blocks `ALTER TABLE ... ADD COLUMN` with NOT NULL on tables that already have rows — there's no value to fill in for existing rows.\n\nScope:\n- `DEFAULT` clause in CREATE TABLE and ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN\n- Persist default expressions in the schema (extend `schemaDisk` / `columnDisk`)\n- Apply defaults on INSERT when a column is omitted\n- Apply defaults to existing rows when ADD COLUMN with NOT NULL + DEFAULT is used\n- `validateSchema` currently rejects Default columns — lift that restriction\n\nThis also unblocks ADD NOT NULL columns on populated tables in rdb-cf0385.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aD","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-68106e","target_id":"rdb-cf0385","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature"]},"created_at":"2026-09-14T07:44:59.205893Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
