{"id":"rdb-cab03f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a98999c8-e54d-4b64-946a-6f6cf2741d27","text":"Implementation complete. Changes in `engine/catalog.go`:\n\n1. Added `Collation string` field to `columnDisk` with `json:\"collation,omitempty\"` — stores the collation name (e.g. `\"utf8mb4_general_ci\"`), empty/absent for default.\n2. `encodeSchema()` — extracts collation from `StringType` and `EnumType`, stores name when non-default.\n3. `decodeType()` — new `collation sql.CollationID` parameter, used for string and ENUM type creation instead of hardcoded `Collation_Default`.\n4. `decodeSchema()` — resolves collation string via `sql.ParseCollation`, defaults to `Collation_Default` when absent (backwards compat).\n5. `validateSchema()` — extracts collation from both string and enum types, removed the ENUM non-default collation rejection.\n\n5 new tests in `engine_test.go`:\n- `TestCollationCaseInsensitiveWhere` — WHERE with case mismatch matches on `utf8mb4_general_ci`\n- `TestCollationCaseInsensitiveOrderBy` — ORDER BY sorts case-insensitively\n- `TestCollationPersistsThroughReopen` — collation survives close/reopen, visible in SHOW CREATE TABLE\n- `TestCollationDefaultBackwardsCompat` — default collation remains case-sensitive after reopen\n- `TestEnumWithCollation` — ENUM with non-default collation accepted and round-trips through reopen\n\nFull test suite passes."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:10:16.935608Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-cab03f","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:46:10.332452Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-cab03f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-07f7876e-982d-492d-b6e3-0b261b8d7850","text":"Addressed P1 review finding — collated string primary keys now use weight strings for key encoding.\n\n**Additional change in `encodeKey()` (catalog.go):** For string PK columns with non-default collation, `encodeKey` now calls `CollationID.WriteWeightString()` to produce collation-aware key bytes. This ensures \"Alice\" and \"alice\" map to the same key under `utf8mb4_general_ci`, enforcing PK uniqueness and enabling correct lookups.\n\n**3 new PK tests:**\n- `TestCollationStringPKUniqueness` — inserting case-variant of existing PK is rejected as duplicate\n- `TestCollationStringPKLookup` — WHERE on PK matches case-insensitively\n- `TestCollationStringPKPersistsThroughReopen` — both behaviors survive close/reopen\n\nFull suite passes (8 total collation tests, all green)."},"created_at":"2026-09-15T08:47:29.97387Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
